        "text": {
            "description_html": "<b>Fusion AR-Z8, Elite Collection Virginia Lever with Rope Rose</b>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\nThe Virginia Lever with Rope Rosette has a classic shape with traditional rope detailing along the edge that really makes it stand out. The lever itself is comfortable in the hand while the rope rose brings an elegance that really makes it something special. The Virginia Leverset will fit 1-1/4 inch to 2 inch thick doors and has an adjustable backset for either 2-3/8 inches or 2-3/4 inches; and since it is part of Fusion's Elite Collection, it has concealed screw mounting for a polished look once installed.\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\n<b>Features</b> of the Fusion AR-Z8 Traditional Virginia Leverset:\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Solid Brass/Bronze Construction</li>\r\n<li>Cycle Tested to ANSI Standards</li>\r\n<li>Exclusive Fusion lever spring assembly for lifetime performance.</li>\r\n<li>Reversible Latchbolt in matching/coordinating finish.</li>\r\n<li>Easy assembly with alignment block and rose posts.</li>\r\n<li>Concealed screw rose cover.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\n<b>Specifications</b> for the Wave Lever with Rope Detailing:\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Lever Length: 4-1/5\"</li>\r\n<li>Projection: 2-3/5\"</li>\r\n<li>Rose Diameter: 2-5/8\"</li>\r\n<li>Door Thickness: adjustable for 1-3/8\" to 2\"</li>\r\n<li>Backset: adjustable for 2-3/8\" to 2-3/4\"</li>\r\n<li>Material: Solid Brass and Bronze</li>\r\n<li>Standard Latch Rotation is 40 Degrees.</li>\r\n<li>Square corner latches and strike plates.</li>\r\n<li>Lifetime Limited Warranty on workmanship, materials, and operation.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\n<b>When Selecting a Function:</b>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><b>Single Dummy:</b> Non-functional pull to match trim on one side of the door. Just for looks, it does not latch and does not lock.</li>\r\n<li><b>Dummy Set:</b> Non-functional pull to match trim on both sides of the door. Just for looks, it does not latch and does not lock.</li>\r\n<li><b>Passage (Hall or Closet):</b> For doors that don't need locking.</li>\r\n<li><b>Privacy (Bedroom or Bathroom):</b> For doors that could need locking.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\n<b>Note: The Single Dummy Function is Handed</b>. All other functions are non-handed. <a href=\"/pages/how-to-order-door-hardware\"><b>Handing Guide</b></a>\r\n</p>",
